Styling footnotes separately from source notes lets you visually distinguish the two sections.
Here we apply different background fills to each.

::: {#607b3494 .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
(
    GT(gtcars_mini)
    .tab_footnote(
        footnote="Prices in USD.",
        locations=loc.column_labels(columns="msrp")
    )
    .tab_footnote(
        footnote="All models from 2017.",
        locations=None
    )
    .tab_source_note(source_note="From edmunds.com")
    .tab_style(
        style=style.fill(color="#FFFFDD"),
        locations=loc.footnotes()
    )
    .tab_style(
        style=style.fill(color="#DDECFF"),
        locations=loc.source_notes()
    )
)
```

